<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huaca Loro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huaca Loro is an adobe pyramid in the Sicán Precinct at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batan-grande">Batán Grande</a> on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, built during the Middle Sicán period of about 900–1100. Excavations led by Izumi Shimada in the early 1990s uncovered its East Tomb, the burial of a lord with large quantities of gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and other precious objects, revealing the wealth of the Sicán elite.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huaca-loro.jpg" alt="Huaca Loro" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sican123 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grantocadolambayeque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
